## Intuition
The problem asks us to insert a new interval into an existing list of intervals and merge any overlapping intervals.

This can be viewed as a variation of the classic Merge Intervals problem.

The key idea is:

Add the new interval to the list.

Sort all intervals based on their starting time.

Traverse the sorted intervals and merge overlapping ones.

If the current interval overlaps with the previous one, we merge them.
If it does not overlap, we store the previous interval and move forward.

